<GuideLayout 
  title="Factory Audit Checklist for Activewear Importers"
  description="Don't leave your brand's reputation to chance. Use this professional audit checklist to verify your activewear manufacturing partner."
  publishDate="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>An effective factory audit is about more than just checking machines. It's about verifying the systems that ensure consistency over thousands of units. Here is the essential checklist we recommend for all B2B activewear importers.</p>

  <h2>1. Quality Management Systems (QMS)</h2>
  <p>Does the factory have an in-house fabric testing lab? At Fitclo, we test every roll of fabric for color fastness, shrinkage, and pilling before a single cut is made. Verification of an ISO 9001 or similar system is a must.</p>

  <h2>2. Social Responsibility & Compliance</h2>
  <p>Verify certifications like BSCI or Sedex. Ethical manufacturing is not just a moral choice; it's a legal requirement for selling in major markets like the EU and North America. Ensure the factory provides raw video evidence of working conditions.</p>

  <h2>3. Technical Capability Check</h2>
  <p>Specific machines for flatlock stitching and automated fabric spreaders are indicators of a high-end facility. A factory's ability to provide 100% inspection on finished goods is what separates professional partners from low-cost workshops.</p>

</GuideLayout>
